# Security headers, served by Cloudflare Pages (this file ships in
# dist-web/ like every other public/ asset; Pages reads it from the
# build output). Test: scripts/test-service-worker.mjs asserts it
# survives the build.
#
# ACTIVE below: the headers that cannot break the app.
# - frame-ancestors/X-Frame-Options: nothing embeds this app in a
#   frame, and a planner is exactly the kind of thing clickjacking
#   likes.
# - nosniff: the build serves correct content types.
# - Referrer-Policy no-referrer: URLs here can carry a recovery token
#   in the hash; hashes are never sent in Referer, but no-referrer
#   costs nothing and removes the whole question.
# - Permissions-Policy: the app uses the microphone (recording) and
#   nothing else on the list; everything unused is denied.
#
# PROPOSED, NOT ACTIVE — Content-Security-Policy. The policy below is
# what the app can actually run under today; it is commented out
# pending Jared's ruling because two allowances in it deserve a
# decision rather than a default:
#
#   Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; connect-src 'self' https://kuhtogvewcooigudmgwj.supabase.co; img-src 'self' data:; media-src 'self' blob:; worker-src 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'
#
# What each allowance is for, and what tightening would break:
# - script-src 'unsafe-inline': index.html carries two inline scripts
#   ON PURPOSE (the pre-paint dark-mode block and the sw-register
#   block). Dropping 'unsafe-inline' breaks both — dark mode flashes
#   and the worker never registers. The tightening path is CSP hashes,
#   which the build would need to compute per release since the
#   blocks' bytes are part of index.html; doable, not free.
# - style-src 'unsafe-inline': React style attributes (folder colours,
#   theme accents) are inline styles; without it every coloured chip
#   goes unstyled.
# - connect-src: the Supabase project URL, which is in config.js. If
#   the project ever moves, this line is a second place that names it.
# - media-src blob:: the recording review screen plays back the
#   just-recorded audio from a blob URL.
# - The pages.dev PREVIEWS get these same headers (one file, every
#   deploy), which is fine: same app, same backend.

/*
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
  Permissions-Policy: microphone=(self), camera=(self), geolocation=(), payment=(), usb=()
